Attribution
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Snakecharmer's Razer HID protocol implementation is derived from OpenRazer:

    OpenRazer — https://github.com/openrazer/openrazer
    Referenced sources carry SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later.

Specifically, the report structure, CRC, transaction IDs, command classes, and
Chroma matrix-effect encodings in the `razer-proto` crate are derived from the
following OpenRazer sources:

    driver/razercommon.c
    driver/razercommon.h
    driver/razerchromacommon.c
    driver/razermouse_driver.c
    driver/razermouse_driver.h
    daemon/openrazer_daemon/hardware/mouse.py

Reference snapshot reviewed on 2026-10-26:
    https://github.com/openrazer/openrazer/tree/477f4d6d3ab7e9deb6310d5bd3742560c5cbe80d
Exact file identities: reference/openrazer-source.json.

This is a later source review, not a record of the original port's unrecorded
revision or a new hardware verification. It found a DPI-write selector mismatch:
the pinned helper emits VARSTORE (0x01), while Snakecharmer emits 0x00. Extended
polling also omits the reference driver's second selector-0x01 request. See
docs/SPEC.md, "Reference snapshot", for the scope and unresolved differences.
Existing byte tests assert Snakecharmer's chosen reports; they do not establish
that every report is identical to this snapshot's output.

OpenRazer is the work of its many contributors and performed the original
reverse-engineering of Razer's USB HID control protocol. Snakecharmer would not exist
without it. This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by the OpenRazer
project.

